WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:17.850
"What's a show shirt?" Cole asked.

2
00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:24.324
"It's a special kind of shirt that you wear under your show coat," Daisy said with a frown.

3
00:00:24.325 --> 00:00:27.691
"Mine was hanging by my pony's stall earlier.

4
00:00:27.692 --> 00:00:33.092
But when I went back there just now to get changed, it was gone!"

5
00:00:33.093 --> 00:00:36.905
"Is your show coat missing too?" Henry asked.

6
00:00:36.906 --> 00:00:43.803
"No, it's just her shirt," Maggie said. "Don't worry, Daisy," she went on.

7
00:00:43.804 --> 00:00:46.764
"The Lemonade Detectives are on the case!"

8
00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:50.106
"Thanks." Daisy still looked worried.

9
00:00:50.107 --> 00:00:54.771
"I really hope you can solve the mystery before my first class.

10
00:00:54.772 --> 00:01:00.892
I'll never win a blue ribbon if I'm wearing this!" She pointed to her T-shirt.

11
00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:05.805
"Ms. Wood said fancy clothes aren't mandatory," Maggie reminded her.

12
00:01:05.806 --> 00:01:08.116
"You just told me that."

13
00:01:08.117 --> 00:01:13.111
"I know," Daisy said. But she still looked worried.

14
00:01:13.112 --> 00:01:16.772
"What does your shirt look like?" Henry asked.

15
00:01:16.773 --> 00:01:22.707
"It's mostly white, with long sleeves and a high collar," Daisy said.

16
00:01:22.708 --> 00:01:29.303
"There's a pocket in the front with a strip of pink and yellow polka-dotted ribbon across the top."

17
00:01:29.304 --> 00:01:31.027
Henry looked around.

18
00:01:31.028 --> 00:01:35.675
A lot of the other riders were wearing long-sleeved white shirts with high collars.

19
00:01:35.676 --> 00:01:38.347
But none of them had pockets like that.

20
00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:42.804
"It sounds like your shirt will be easy to spot," he told Daisy.

21
00:01:42.805 --> 00:01:44.909
"We'll see what we can do."

22
00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:48.288
"Thanks." Daisy sounded distracted.

23
00:01:48.289 --> 00:01:55.242
"I'd better go see if anyone has an extra shirt I can borrow, just in case."

24
00:01:55.243 --> 00:01:59.438
"Are you guys crazy?" Cole said after Daisy left.

25
00:01:59.439 --> 00:02:02.273
"We don't have time to solve a mystery today.

26
00:02:02.274 --> 00:02:05.483
We're supposed to be selling lemonade!"

27
00:02:05.484 --> 00:02:08.707
"We can do both." Maggie sounded excited.

28
00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:14.325
"If we solve the case quickly, maybe I can use the detective fee to enter more classes!"

29
00:02:14.326 --> 00:02:17.311
Cole frowned but didn't say anything else.

30
00:02:17.312 --> 00:02:21.037
Henry wondered if he was thinking about swim team practice.

31
00:02:21.038 --> 00:02:25.527
Cole loved being on the swim team, and he hated to miss a practice.

32
00:02:25.528 --> 00:02:31.085
If they finished early at the show, Cole might have time to get to the pool for part of today's practice.

33
00:02:31.086 --> 00:02:35.329
But that probably wouldn't happen if they were busy trying to solve a mystery.

34
00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:38.744
"I agree with Maggie," Henry told Cole.

35
00:02:38.745 --> 00:02:44.387
"I think we should try to solve the case. Daisy seems really upset."

36
00:02:44.388 --> 00:02:47.772
"Good, then let's get started," Maggie said.

37
00:02:47.773 --> 00:02:54.213
"Why don't we—" She stopped talking when Ms. Wood hurried up to the lemonade stand.

38
00:02:54.214 --> 00:02:57.768
"There you are, Maggie," the stable owner said.

39
00:02:57.769 --> 00:03:01.502
"It's time to get Big Spot ready for your first class."

40
00:03:01.503 --> 00:03:04.963
"Oh, right." Maggie slapped her forehead.

41
00:03:04.964 --> 00:03:08.725
"Sorry, Ms. Wood. I got distracted."

42
00:03:08.726 --> 00:03:12.985
She started to follow Ms. Wood toward the barn.

43
00:03:12.986 --> 00:03:19.101
Then she rushed back to the lemonade stand and whispered, "You guys should start investigating!"

44
00:03:19.102 --> 00:03:24.073
Henry nodded as Maggie hurried off again. "Okay," he said to Cole.

45
00:03:24.074 --> 00:03:27.825
"We should start by checking out the scene of the crime.

46
00:03:27.826 --> 00:03:30.866
Maybe the thief left some clues."

47
00:03:30.867 --> 00:03:35.720
Cole glanced past him. "Here come some more customers," he said.

48
00:03:35.721 --> 00:03:39.088
"Why don't you serve them while I go look for clues in the barn?"

49
00:03:39.089 --> 00:03:43.140
Henry was surprised that Cole was volunteering to look for clues.

50
00:03:43.141 --> 00:03:46.222
Cole hadn't seemed very interested in the case.

51
00:03:46.223 --> 00:03:50.075
But Cole rushed off before Henry could say anything about that.

52
00:03:50.076 --> 00:03:55.448
"One lemonade, please!" a little boy cried, tossing a quarter on the table.

53
00:03:55.449 --> 00:03:59.149
"You got it," Henry said, reaching for the nearest pitcher.

54
00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:02.986
For the next few minutes, he was too busy to think about the case.

55
00:04:02.987 --> 00:04:07.227
Finally the latest group of lemonade customers had all been served.

56
00:04:07.228 --> 00:04:09.446
Henry looked over toward the barn.

57
00:04:09.447 --> 00:04:13.137
Henry guessed that Cole was still inside looking for clues.

58
00:04:13.138 --> 00:04:15.453
He thought about going to help him.

59
00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:19.715
But he wasn't sure he should leave the lemonade stand.

60
00:04:19.716 --> 00:04:23.368
Then he spotted Daisy walking past, leading a pony.

61
00:04:23.369 --> 00:04:27.740
The pony was a little taller than Maggie's favorite pony, Big Spot.

62
00:04:27.741 --> 00:04:31.607
It had a glossy brown coat and a black mane and tail.

63
00:04:31.608 --> 00:04:36.585
Daisy led the pony into the shade of some tall trees nearby.

64
00:04:36.586 --> 00:04:41.080
She leaned against one of the trees, and the pony began to graze.

65
00:04:41.081 --> 00:04:45.576
Henry looked around to make sure no more lemonade customers were coming.

66
00:04:45.577 --> 00:04:49.382
Then he left the lemonade stand and hurried over to Daisy.

67
00:04:49.383 --> 00:04:53.277
"Hi," he said. "What are you doing?"

68
00:04:53.278 --> 00:04:58.757
"Coco likes to roll in her stall," Daisy said, gesturing toward the grazing pony.

69
00:04:58.758 --> 00:05:03.980
"I'm trying to keep her moving so she doesn't get dirty before our classes.

70
00:05:03.981 --> 00:05:06.850
Did you find my show shirt yet?"

71
00:05:06.851 --> 00:05:09.593
"We're working on it," Henry said.

72
00:05:09.594 --> 00:05:13.358
He opened his mouth to ask her more questions about her show shirt.

73
00:05:13.359 --> 00:05:16.385
But then he noticed someone rushing toward them.

74
00:05:16.386 --> 00:05:22.171
It was a girl around Daisy's age with a long blond braid. She looked angry.

75
00:05:22.172 --> 00:05:26.640
"Hey!" the girl yelled, ignoring Henry and pointing a finger at Daisy.

76
00:05:26.641 --> 00:05:32.111
"You stole my pony!"
